{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "26105572",
      "title": "Diving into Functions & Function Types",
      "lectureOrder": 757,
      "videoOrder": 697,
      "sourceHash": "108e1b084d4b6da05c7f613454a5ff7ad3c8031b8c54414d034f0cb1dc360144",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 3.09,
          "en": "Instructor: Now, there are a lot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.09,
          "end": 5.91,
          "en": "of other core TypeScript features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.91,
          "end": 8.13,
          "en": "which I do explore in greater detail",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.13,
          "end": 10.05,
          "en": "in my TypeScript course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.05,
          "end": 13.32,
          "en": "To come to an end here for this introduction,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.32,
          "end": 18.15,
          "en": "there are just two last features which I wanna cover here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.15,
          "end": 21.87,
          "en": "and that would be functions combined with types",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.87,
          "end": 25.2,
          "en": "and then thereafter generic types.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.2,
          "end": 29.73,
          "en": "Let's start with functions and types,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.73,
          "end": 31.98,
          "en": "and I'm saying function and types",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.98,
          "end": 34.71,
          "en": "because when we work with functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.71,
          "end": 39.243,
          "en": "there are different places where types can be assigned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.17,
          "end": 41.97,
          "en": "Let's start by adding a function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.97,
          "end": 45.213,
          "en": "Let's say the add function again, which we saw before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.23,
          "end": 49.92,
          "en": "The add function can get parameters, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.92,
          "end": 53.52,
          "en": "like any function, just as I did it before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.52,
          "end": 57.03,
          "en": "and then for these parameters, we can assign types.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.03,
          "end": 61.71,
          "en": "That's what we saw before here in this first example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.71,
          "end": 64.77,
          "en": "Just as we can set types for variables,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.77,
          "end": 67.86,
          "en": "we can also set types for parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.86,
          "end": 71.97,
          "en": "We can make it clear that here we wanna allow numbers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.97,
          "end": 76.413,
          "en": "for example, and then I can return a plus b.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 77.78999999999999,
          "end": 81.93,
          "en": "But with that we also have one inferred type here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 81.93,
          "end": 83.13,
          "en": "in this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 83.13,
          "end": 87.393,
          "en": "and do you see where we're using type inference here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 88.47,
          "end": 92.13,
          "en": "Well, here in this function I am returning a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 92.13,
          "end": 97.13,
          "en": "and that tells TypeScript something about the return type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 97.28999999999999,
          "end": 100.74000000000001,
          "en": "the type of the returned value of this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 100.74000000000001,
          "end": 103.68,
          "en": "and it infers this type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 103.68,
          "end": 107.88,
          "en": "We can see the type it infers if we hover over add,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 107.88,
          "end": 111.6,
          "en": "then we see the TypeScript definition of this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 111.6,
          "end": 114.36,
          "en": "and we see that of course, for the parameters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 114.36,
          "end": 116.7,
          "en": "we have the two types we set up,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 116.7,
          "end": 119.61,
          "en": "the number types, but then here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 119.61,
          "end": 123.12,
          "en": "after this function name and the parameter list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 123.12,
          "end": 126.09,
          "en": "this colon here and this type here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 126.09,
          "end": 127.68,
          "en": "that's not coming from us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 127.68,
          "end": 129.54,
          "en": "We haven't edited this code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 129.54,
          "end": 133.65,
          "en": "Instead, that's the inferred return value type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 133.65,
          "end": 135.9,
          "en": "TypeScript infers here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 135.9,
          "end": 140.7,
          "en": "So TypeScript knows that here it will get a number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 140.7,
          "end": 144.66,
          "en": "as a return value because it sees that this code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 144.66,
          "end": 147.57,
          "en": "with these parameters, which are always",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 147.57,
          "end": 150.51,
          "en": "of type number can only return a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 150.51,
          "end": 153.69,
          "en": "There's no other value that could be returned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 153.69,
          "end": 157.98,
          "en": "And that's why this number return value is inferred.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 157.98,
          "end": 160.65,
          "en": "We could also explicitly set it though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 160.65,
          "end": 165.65,
          "en": "We can set the return type of a function by adding a colon",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 166.05,
          "end": 168.72,
          "en": "after this function parameter list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 168.72,
          "end": 170.97,
          "en": "and then setting the return type here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 170.97,
          "end": 174.72,
          "en": "like number or string or a union type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 174.72,
          "end": 176.34300000000002,
          "en": "that would also be possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 177.66,
          "end": 179.49,
          "en": "That's something we can do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 179.49,
          "end": 181.05,
          "en": "But just as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 181.05,
          "end": 183.33,
          "en": "if you don't have a reason for doing that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 183.33,
          "end": 184.68,
          "en": "you shouldn't do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 184.68,
          "end": 187.2,
          "en": "TypeScript already infers a type here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 187.2,
          "end": 189.72,
          "en": "and if that's the type you wanna stick to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 189.72,
          "end": 194.01,
          "en": "then there's no need to explicitly define it yourself.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 194.01,
          "end": 195.9,
          "en": "Still, I wanna mention this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 195.9,
          "end": 200.37,
          "en": "that functions when we work with types, don't just use types",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 200.37,
          "end": 204.21,
          "en": "for the parameters, but also for the return value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 204.21,
          "end": 207.42000000000002,
          "en": "That's easy to overlook, but it makes a lot of sense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 207.42000000000002,
          "end": 211.82999999999998,
          "en": "because a function after all, does not have just some input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 211.82999999999998,
          "end": 215.673,
          "en": "it also has some output and hence it has a return type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 216.66,
          "end": 218.76,
          "en": "Now, there is a special return type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 218.76,
          "end": 220.68,
          "en": "which is all the worth knowing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 220.68,
          "end": 221.79,
          "en": "And for that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 221.79,
          "end": 225.84,
          "en": "let me add a print function where I get a value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 225.84,
          "end": 228.21,
          "en": "and that could indeed be of type any,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 228.21,
          "end": 229.77,
          "en": "because the only thing I'll do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 229.77,
          "end": 233.19,
          "en": "with that value is I'll console.log it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 233.19,
          "end": 234.32999999999998,
          "en": "So I don't really care",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 234.32999999999998,
          "end": 239.32999999999998,
          "en": "about the concrete type of this value, I'm just logging it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 239.49,
          "end": 240.63,
          "en": "Now, one important note",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 240.63,
          "end": 243.21,
          "en": "about naming this function print though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 243.21,
          "end": 245.82,
          "en": "which I unfortunately only discovered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 245.82,
          "end": 248.07,
          "en": "after I named the function like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 248.07,
          "end": 249.6,
          "en": "of course, in JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 249.6,
          "end": 252.6,
          "en": "there is a built-in print function already,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 252.6,
          "end": 256.11,
          "en": "so now this function will clash with this built-in function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 256.11,
          "end": 259.8,
          "en": "and hence if you would try to compile this TypeScript file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 259.8,
          "end": 262.17,
          "en": "you would be getting an error because of that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 262.17,
          "end": 264.19,
          "en": "so maybe just name it, print_output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 265.17,
          "end": 268.98,
          "en": "or something like that to avoid that error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 268.98,
          "end": 272.4,
          "en": "But the important thing about this print function now is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 272.4,
          "end": 276.48,
          "en": "that this function does not return anything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 276.48,
          "end": 278.85,
          "en": "it has no return statement,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 278.85,
          "end": 283.213,
          "en": "and therefore it has a special return type called void.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 285.63,
          "end": 290.01,
          "en": "Void is basically comparable to null and undefined,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 290.01,
          "end": 292.95,
          "en": "but it's only used in conjunction with functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 292.95,
          "end": 297.24,
          "en": "and it means that this function never returns.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 297.24,
          "end": 299.82,
          "en": "So, if I wanna work with the returned value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 299.82,
          "end": 303.6,
          "en": "from that function, I will work with undefined,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 303.6,
          "end": 307.38,
          "en": "and that's that special void type for functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 307.38,
          "end": 310.14300000000003,
          "en": "for the return value of functions.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
